2g1g|n|A garment; clothing; especially, an upper or outer garment. ; An article of dress worn in token of grief; a mourning garment or badge; as, he wore a weed on his hat; especially, in the plural, mourning garb, as of a woman; as, a widow's weeds. ; A sudden illness or relapse, often attended with fever, which attacks women in childbed. ; Underbrush; low shrubs. ; Any plant growing in cultivated ground to the injury of the crop or desired vegetation, or to the disfigurement of the place; an unsightly, useless, or injurious plant. ; Fig.: Something unprofitable or troublesome; anything useless. ; An animal unfit to breed from. ; Tobacco, or a cigar.	v:21yh,111,4;21y8,86,1~21yh,111,4;21y8,86,1	n:21y8,86,1~21y8,86,1
